498	/**
499	 * Decide the runtime plan from an era-cell provision, by reading the disk.
500	 *
501	 * The question asked of the provision is the only one that can be answered
502	 * here: does its `location` name a runtime tree in this checkout that carries
503	 * `bin/node`? The workspace runtime cache spells its locations relative to the
504	 * checkout, so it does. The running process spells its location as a sentence
505	 * about itself, and a version manager spells its location relative to that
506	 * manager's own root — neither resolves here, and neither is guessed at. Both
507	 * fall to `host`, which is what the child would have got anyway, and the
508	 * supplier and version the stage named are still carried so the row says which
509	 * provision it was that could not be prepended.
